## Still uncovered

**Golden SAML** — no Splunk ES rule exists. Searched and found nothing. The attack happens at the ADFS/federation layer, which is why neither MDI nor our existing content sees it. Would need Entra ID logs in Splunk and a custom rule.

**Entra Connect compromise** — same position. Hybrid identity telemetry we don't currently have.

**MachineAccountQuota compromise** — no MDI detection and no existing rule. Detectable via event 4741 filtered to non-admin account creation, but would need building.

## Two issues affecting all of the above

- **Automatic Windows auditing configuration is off** in the Defender portal (Settings → Identities → Advanced features). MDI depends on Windows events to produce these detections.
- **[DC name] has no MDI sensor.** Activity against that DC isn't visible to MDI at all.

Until both are resolved, the coverage in the table above is what we're licensed for, not what we're actually getting.
